# Superpowers — opt-in only

The Superpowers Cursor plugin is installed, but its **automatic workflow is disabled for this repo**.

## Default (every task)

- Do **not** invoke `superpowers:*` process skills on your own.
- Do **not** run brainstorm → spec → plan unless the user opted in.
- Do **not** create `docs/superpowers/**` — **retired**. Never write there.
- Work normally: use repo `.cursor/rules/` and `.cursor/skills/` as needed.

## When Superpowers is allowed

Only when the user runs **`/superpowers-*`** or explicitly asks for Superpowers.

Then follow the referenced Superpowers skill **and** **`.agent/skills/superpowers/SKILL.md`** for save locations and **§ Lean mode** (hooks block subagents for plan/brainstorm/debug):

| Plugin default (ignore)   | Use instead                  |
| ------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| `docs/superpowers/plans/` | **`docs/workflow/planned/`** |
| `docs/superpowers/specs/` | **`docs/workflow/intake/`**  |

Update `docs/workflow/planned/README.md` when adding a plan. Use `/workflow-start` before implementation.

Prefer a **single** brainstorm/plan pass — hooks enforce no subagent fan-out on all `/superpowers-*` commands (including execute).

## Precedence

This rule overrides the Superpowers plugin session bootstrap. User instructions always win.
